1
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:45,211
Are you here? Are you following me?

2
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,720
Agent Alex? What do you need?

3
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,346
I have someone
you have to background check.

4
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,890
Okay… Who?

5
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:58,641
Everyone here in Mikoy's place.

6
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,894
Everyone, from Captain Pepe to Rahmboy.

7
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,938
I'll explain later.
Just do it, Agent Dara.

8
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,815
- Okay, copy.
- Thank you.

9
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:10,528
He just entered a new relationship,
he already forgot about me.

10
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:17,911
Let's say I'm not good at keeping secrets.

11
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,454
What secret is that?

12
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,625
<i>It depends.</i>

13
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,251
<i>What you were thinking is wrong.</i>

14
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:29,297
Honestly, Senator Quintin is not in ill.

15
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:31,382
What he have is a dream.

16
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,761
I thought it was just his hair
that he wanted to bring back.

17
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:38,348
Turns out it's an organization.
The Sinigang Cartel 2.0.

18
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:44,979
And that's everything
the doctor said, sir.

19
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:50,693
If Senator Quintin
manages to carry out his plans,

20
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,822
he's not just planning to take down
the Moravianos,

21
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:58,326
he's slowly building Sinigang Cartel 2.0.

22
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:02,914
Who else knows about this?

23
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:04,290
Just us.

24
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:07,669
Me, Carlota, Cocoy, and you, sir.

25
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:12,090
Should we tell Agent Alex?

26
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:13,508
Maybe she can help.

27
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:14,509
No.

28
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:19,222
No one else should know about this.

29
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:22,892
We don't know how deep this goes.

30
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:26,896
What if everything
the doctor said is true?

31
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:30,316
Then we have even
more reason to stay quiet.

32
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,737
If we're wrong,

33
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:36,906
the senator will just run.

34
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:38,950
He'll go into hiding.

35
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:42,453
And if we're right,

36
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:45,957
then we can't afford to make a mistake.

37
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:55,550
And within the four walls

38
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:57,802
of this office.

39
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:02,473
No one should know about this. Clear?

40
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:04,350
Crystal clear, sir.

41
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:07,145
Yes, sir.

42
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:12,609
So it's not just
the senator we're watching.

43
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:17,572
We're also watching
a new syndicate being born.

44
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:32,211
Looks like you're doing well
under house arrest.

45
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,714
But I hope you haven't had it too hard.

46
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:40,428
You are powerful enough to get me out

47
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:43,181
just for this meal.

48
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:48,937
But you can't make my charges disappear?

49
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,605
Come on.

50
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:53,483
I can't make your charges disappear.

51
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:55,443
It'd be too obvious.

52
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:03,660
But there is something else I can erase.

53
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,080
You.

54
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:16,923
And no one will come after you.

55
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:21,594
And you'll be protected,
along with Donabel.

56
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:24,055
What's the catch?

57
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,018
Chiara.

58
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:30,436
Chiara?

59
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:32,855
Why?

60
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:36,276
What do you need her for?

61
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:42,073
There's only one target.

62
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:48,413
<i>The President</i>
<i>of the Republic of the Philippines.</i>

63
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:36,461
Do you need goggles and a life vest?

64
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,214
You're thinking about the Pacific Ocean.

65
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:42,091
It's deep.

66
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:44,552
Nothing.

67
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:50,349
There's just so much
to take care of for the wedding.

68
00:05:56,147 --> 00:05:58,775
All the guests we've invited.

69
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,360
And then there's our first dance.

70
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:04,989
Weddings really are stressful, huh?

71
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:13,206
Oh, no.

72
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,708
Poor sweetheart.

73
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,169
You're so stressed.

74
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:23,007
I think you need to relax, sweetheart.

75
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:29,555
You know, sweetheart,

76
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:33,976
I think I have an idea
that might help you…

77
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:35,937
relax.

78
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:37,772
Oh, boy.

79
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:40,650
There you go again with your suggestions!

80
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:41,609
Why?

81
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:43,402
Looks like I'll be up late tonight.

82
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,491
Just kidding.

83
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:50,243
Oh, you.

84
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:53,329
Don't stress yourself out, okay?

85
00:07:01,337 --> 00:07:03,464
- Did Alex call you?
- Yup.

86
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:09,303
How is she? Why did she call?

87
00:07:09,387 --> 00:07:10,221
Well,

88
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,765
she just asked me to check if

89
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:16,644
there's anything suspicious
around our two stars.

90
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:19,522
Around Mikoy and Chiara.

91
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:20,982
Why?

92
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:23,818
Well, nothing. Typical Agent Alex.

93
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:28,906
But she's right because

94
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:32,034
the two of them
used to be high-value assets.

95
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:36,706
So, it's understandable
that she just wants to make sure

96
00:07:36,789 --> 00:07:38,541
Mikoy and Chiara are safe.

97
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,084
True.

98
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:42,462
You know what's funny?

99
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,630
Because you said "our stars".

100
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:47,216
- That's so typical of soap operas, right?
- Why?

101
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,843
That on the actual wedding day,

102
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:53,014
so many issues end up happening
on the wedding day itself.

103
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:55,475
- Exactly, exactly.
- Makes sense, makes sense.

104
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:58,519
But speaking of the wedding,
are you invited?

105
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:03,858
Well, I'm assuming I'm invited because

106
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:07,153
I've become a big part
of Mikoy and Chiara's lives.

107
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,490
So you're assuming too.

108
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:12,575
Why? What about you?

109
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:13,993
Are you invited?

110
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:14,994
No.

111
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:18,831
But I'm not going to assume I'm invited,

112
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:19,874
like you.

113
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:51,447
Since when have you been making moves
on your own without me knowing?

114
00:08:53,407 --> 00:08:55,743
Since when have
you been working with Cocoy

115
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:58,496
to independently investigate
Senator Quintin?

116
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:09,882
You said it yourself,

117
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,592
be proactive.

118
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:14,762
One of the habits
of highly effective people.

119
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:25,856
And I just want to remind you,

120
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,402
Carlota, you are standing on thin ice,

121
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,322
because of your complicated background.

122
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:36,325
So here at the agency,

123
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:39,537
it's very easy to think that you're acting
like a rogue agent

124
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,622
because of things like this.

125
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:43,291
Especially if you don't tell anyone,

126
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:46,544
and your higher-ups don't know
what you're doing.

127
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:48,796
I'm sorry.

128
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:51,799
I just thought it would be better

129
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:53,509
if I took the initiative

130
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:56,721
and found out
who this agency's enemies are.

131
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,024
Tell me right away.

132
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:10,234
Because I want to know what you're doing.

133
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:14,780
So I know how I can protect you better.

134
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:44,268
You know, Mikoy, Chiara,

135
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:49,398
in life, there are so
many things we can't control,

136
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:51,776
no matter how much we prepare.

137
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:57,239
So instead of stressing over
the things we can't control,

138
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:58,324
um…

139
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:00,242
let's relax!

140
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,703
- There you go!
- Hang out, have a chat!

141
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:04,288
And zone out!

142
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:08,125
See?

143
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:11,295
Sometimes it's better to slow down.

144
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:13,547
Just have a few drinks and chill.

145
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:16,634
So, Mikoy, Chiara, cheers!

146
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,177
Nice!

147
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:19,095
Okay.

148
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:21,597
- What are you doing?
- Joining the drinking.

149
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:24,141
- Why, are you allowed to drink now?
- Exactly.

150
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,643
- I'm not a kid anymore.
- I know.

151
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:28,854
- I'm allowed.
- Wow, do you have a girlfriend now?

152
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:32,942
As for me, I can't.

153
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:34,110
I'm acidic.

154
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:35,736
Oh, that's tough.

155
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,030
- I'm acidic too.
- Really?

156
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:38,948
Yes.

157
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:41,158
All my exes dissolved.

158
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:44,703
There he goes again with the smooth lines!
Looks like you're ready to drink!

159
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:48,833
Maybe there's something
you'd like to drink?

160
00:11:50,584 --> 00:11:52,044
You can have baby girl make it for you.

161
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,379
Yes, right here.

162
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:56,465
Wait.

163
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:57,842
Are you comfortable there?

164
00:11:58,426 --> 00:11:59,969
I'm fine.

165
00:12:01,887 --> 00:12:03,139
- Bro Mikoy.
- Mikoy.

166
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,183
I think Chiara's stressed.

167
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:08,602
Yes, she is.

168
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:11,647
Are you really okay, sweetheart?

169
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:14,275
I know when you're on your period,

170
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,153
your hormones get out of balance.

171
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:20,739
I'm fine. I'm actually happy
that I get to bond with all of you.

172
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,618
I really feel how much
you all care for me.

173
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:25,828
Of course!

174
00:12:25,911 --> 00:12:27,371
That's TLC!

175
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:33,836
And with that,

176
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,963
go all out with your shot, bro Mikoy.

177
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:37,798
All out.

178
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:41,802
I'll take care of the food.

179
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:42,928
- There you go!
- There you go!

180
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:45,431
That's why you're
our absolute favorite, Chiara.

181
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:55,441
Really? He said that?

182
00:12:56,859 --> 00:13:00,821
I don't know whether I should be offended
or take it as sweet.

183
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,825
You call that sweet?

184
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:08,454
Don't you have any emotional maturity?

185
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:10,414
Fair point.

186
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,292
You have a point there, muscle man.

187
00:13:14,793 --> 00:13:20,341
There really is something off
about my boyfriend.

188
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,344
That's strike one for me.

189
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:31,727
That works too.

190
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:39,610
They all carry the same weight for me.

191
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:44,573
What happens when he gets strike three?

192
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:12,643
What happened?

193
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:13,686
Let's go over there.

194
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,567
What happened?

195
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:22,653
Did you find out who the person
helping us is?

196
00:14:30,786 --> 00:14:34,039
The win-win Senator Quintin?

197
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:39,003
What does he want in return?

198
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:46,552
He's offering us a way out,

199
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:49,430
so we can go back to Prague.

200
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:52,224
Just like that?

201
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,685
He can do that?
And why does he want Chiara in return?

202
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,856
Don't tell me he's into our daughter.

203
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:02,693
He's not into our daughter.

204
00:15:02,776 --> 00:15:04,278
What he wants

205
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:07,948
is to overthrow
the President of the Philippines.

206
00:15:11,785 --> 00:15:12,912
What did you say?

207
00:15:16,206 --> 00:15:18,208
So, what do you say?

208
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:25,341
Huh?!

209
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:27,927
You said no?

210
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:33,182
Why are you refusing my kindness?

211
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:46,111
You know, you're a joker.

212
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:48,238
Why don't you become a comedian?

213
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:56,664
I want to start a new life.

214
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:00,125
You know,

215
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:05,297
even if you were reincarnated ten times
and came back to life,

216
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:08,842
or let's make it 20 times,

217
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:12,221
you could never pay for your sins.

218
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:13,973
A bad person,

219
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:17,142
no matter how you turn it around,
is still a bad person.

220
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:23,691
Even if you rot in prison
or even in the afterlife!

221
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:48,048
But we can still change

222
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:52,928
and have a better life

223
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,847
if we atone for our sins.

224
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,893
Is your answer still no?

225
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,940
You don't know me.

226
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,818
I'm a good friend,

227
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:10,404
but I'm a ruthless enemy.

228
00:17:11,363 --> 00:17:13,198
Everything I want,

229
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:15,826
I get.

230
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,758
All right, Mikoy, Chiara.

231
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:32,718
- Take care, bro and sis.
- All right.

232
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:33,969
Take care of Dekyo, okay?

233
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,012
Chiara!

234
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:36,263
Sure.

235
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:39,141
Dekyo, take care of your liver.

236
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:40,434
Say bye first. Bye.

237
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:42,686
- Bye.
- All right, bye, bye, vlog.

238
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:43,604
You two take care.

239
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:44,688
Take care, okay?

240
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:46,106
I'll come with you.

241
00:17:50,027 --> 00:17:51,195
tell me the truth.

242
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,199
What's really stressing you out?

243
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,872
I know you, sweetheart.

244
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:03,373
You're not usually like this.

245
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:08,337
And I feel like this isn't really
about our wedding.

246
00:18:09,254 --> 00:18:11,632
Come on. Tell me, sweetheart.

247
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:13,467
What's really going on?

248
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:25,938
There!

249
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:27,064
See!

250
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:28,941
I knew I was right.

251
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:32,444
That's what you look like
when you're hiding something.

252
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,947
Well, in case you haven't noticed,

253
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,865
after all these years
together, sweetheart,

254
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:37,950
I know you like the back of my hand.

255
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:40,202
I know when you're thinking,

256
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:42,246
when you're making a decision,

257
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:44,790
or when there's something
you're not telling me,

258
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:46,125
like right now.

259
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,918
Come on, sweetheart.

260
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:49,628
It's me.

261
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:52,089
Share that secret of yours.

262
00:18:57,636 --> 00:18:58,804
All right, fine.

263
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:02,349
You're really good at reading people.

264
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:06,979
The truth is,

265
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:11,400
I can't get it out of my head,

266
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:14,444
that CCTV footage Dad Mario showed us.

267
00:19:17,364 --> 00:19:18,365
That?

268
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:23,162
Sweetheart, it's normal for people
to get into fights when they're drinking.

269
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:25,414
You know how it is
when people drink too much.

270
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,124
They end up fighting.

271
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,710
Anyway, sweetheart,

272
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:31,628
when it comes to our wedding,

273
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:34,006
let's all just be happy, okay?

274
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:35,841
Just forget about it.

275
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:40,888
I'm wondering,

276
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:42,890
who could that be?

277
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:46,643
The one who suddenly showed up.

278
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:49,688
Who is that mysterious vigilante?

279
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:53,150
I don't know either.

280
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:54,776
The investigation is still ongoing.

281
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:59,448
Let's just let the local police
handle it, okay?

282
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,950
Besides, Agent Alex is with us.

283
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:05,996
If she notices anything,
she'll probably let us know.

284
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:09,917
You're right.

285
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:16,798
The way he moves,

286
00:20:18,508 --> 00:20:20,886
he's not just some
ordinary guy, sweetheart.

287
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:25,224
It feels familiar.

288
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:29,645
Almost like
the way Donatello and I used to move.

289
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:34,775
I'm almost starting to think I trained
with him in Sicily.

290
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:41,406
Wait, let me correct you there.

291
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,825
Just because he's from Albay

292
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,994
doesn't mean he's not as good as you
when it comes to the moves, right?

293
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:50,540
Maybe the guy is just
naturally talented, right?

294
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:52,542
Besides, don't forget,

295
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,461
Filipinos are world-class
when it comes to talent.

296
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:57,339
So it's possible that, well,

297
00:20:57,422 --> 00:20:59,091
he's just a normal guy, right?

298
00:20:59,716 --> 00:21:03,303
His hidden talent just happened
to come out that night.

299
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:14,022
I'm worried there might be
another threat coming.

300
00:21:15,023 --> 00:21:16,233
Of course,

301
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:19,569
I don't want all of us to get hurt again.

302
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:24,366
La Morte Bianca is gone.

303
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,827
So just relax, okay?

304
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:30,205
Nothing will get in our way anymore.

305
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:34,334
And if there is,

306
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:36,920
I'll show him the moves myself.

307
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:41,341
That's right.

308
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:42,926
I'll take care of it.

309
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,430
Don't stress anymore, okay?

310
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:51,226
Let's go.

311
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:10,037
Goodness!

312
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:13,540
Our enemy is a senator now.

313
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:16,752
How can we possibly go up against him?

314
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:18,712
Even if we know his true colors,

315
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:20,630
he has so many supporters.

316
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:23,008
He's a lawmaker, after all.

317
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:25,552
He can pretty much do whatever he wants.

318
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:27,512
But Viktor.

319
00:22:28,346 --> 00:22:30,682
We can't betray our daughter.

320
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:34,603
We can't trade our freedom
for our daughter's sake.

321
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:38,899
Don't worry.

322
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:42,027
I won't do what he wants.

323
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:06,593
The last thing I want
is another complication for her…

324
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:11,640
in this new chapter
of her life with Mikoy.

325
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:21,191
I won't let Chiara be used again
by people like La Morte Bianca.

326
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:37,541
NORBERTO S. RUIZ
GENERAL

327
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:40,001
I thought you have forgotten about me.

328
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:42,879
You're really something.

329
00:23:43,421 --> 00:23:45,757
I think you're spending
too much time with that Senator.

330
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:47,717
Why did you call?

331
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,930
<i>And I hope you can now be truthful.</i>

332
00:23:57,727 --> 00:23:59,855
Will my family be at peace?

333
00:24:11,491 --> 00:24:13,702
When you involve yourself
with the syndicate,

334
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:17,455
you should always have eyes everywhere.

335
00:24:35,599 --> 00:24:37,976
You really have no originality.

336
00:24:38,059 --> 00:24:40,312
You know what? That's enough!

337
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:47,402
You have to come with us, Viktor Valtrovi.

338
00:24:47,485 --> 00:24:48,695
I'll take care of Sir Viktor!

339
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:49,696
Sir Viktor!

340
00:24:49,779 --> 00:24:50,614
Viktor!

341
00:24:50,697 --> 00:24:53,325
Wherever he is, I should be there as well!

342
00:24:53,408 --> 00:24:54,701
Go inside!

343
00:24:54,784 --> 00:24:56,286
- Go on!
- Wait, be gentle.

344
00:24:56,369 --> 00:24:57,621
That's too much.
